    "description": "CleanCapital is an owner, operator, and investor in distributed clean-energy assets, with a portfolio spanning solar and storage projects. Its customers and counterparties include commercial, industrial, institutional, and utility off-takers that contract for distributed-generation output. The business is asset-heavy and contracted because returns depend on owned operating projects and long-term customer agreements rather than pure development fees. Company materials state that CleanCapital has financed or managed more than 350 projects totaling more than 500 MW across 27 US states and one territory. Its footprint is national, and public financing disclosures indicate more than $1.5 billion of capital mobilized for distributed clean energy. BlackRock announced a financing partnership with the company in 2018 and then made a direct investment in the firm in 2019. Manulife announced a corporate investment in CleanCapital in 2021 and later committed additional capital in 2023.",
